Subject: RE: [S] binding timeSeries together
Message-ID: <5FD4320911EDD21194CB00C04F8EEB1B0878F6@tech_1.mathsoft.co.uk>

The way do do this is with concat().

Example: 

x <- timeSeries( data.frame( a = 1:3, b = 4:6 ), pos=as(1:3, "timeDate"))  
y <- timeSeries( data.frame( a = 7:9, b = 3:5 ), pos=as(11:13, "timeDate"))
concat(x,y)

> concat(x,y)
  Positions a b 
 01/02/1960 1 4
 01/03/1960 2 5
 01/04/1960 3 6
 01/12/1960 7 3
 01/13/1960 8 4
 01/14/1960 9 5

It makes sense for rbind to serve the same purpose, so I'll file an
enhancement request that rbind should work for time series and signal
series.

