Subject: [S] Summary: counting radio stations
Message-ID: <199911181134.LAA14786@ns1.ioi.knaw.nl>

Nick Ellis wrote:

N <- 10
revenue <- rnorm(N,mean=100, sd=10)
market <- factor(sample(1:270, replace=T, 
size=N))
owner <- factor(sample(1:1932, replace=T, 
size=N))
market.owner <- interaction(market,owner,drop=T)
fred <- tapply(revenue, list(market.owner), sum)
df <- 
as.data.frame(c(unpaste(levels(market.owner),sep=
"."),list(fred)))
names(df) <- c("market","owner","sum")
df

Bill Dunlap pointed out that aggregate does 
exactly the same thing! Thus
> aggregate(revenue, list(market, owner), sum)
.....

Sigh. I keep forgetting about aggregate!

I have tried both solutions with N <- 6055
and Nick Ellis's idea produced the result in 
about 20 seconds, whereas aggregate kept going 
on until I got fed up and interrupted the 
process. So it seems that forgetting about 
aggregate is not always a mistake.

