> of the data.  If anyone recognizes it, or knows more,
> please pass it along.

It was in the Venables (and Venables & Smith) Snotes and their datasets. It
comes from S. D. Silvey: "Statistical Inference" (originally Penguin, page
84 in that edition) and I believe it is fictitious.

  On the Aegean island of Kalythos the male inhabitants suffer from a
  congenital eye disease, the effects of which become more marked with
  increasing age.  Samples of islander males of various ages were tested
  for blindness and the results recorded.

A quick web search found that quite a lot of people have versions of
those notes on their Web sites.

